      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "på skolen, på markedet, hjemme",
      "text": "\"Hjemme\" means \"at home\" (when you are there). For the school and the market Norwegian says \"på\": på skolen, på markedet. The ending -en or -et on the noun means \"the\": skolen is \"the school\", markedet is \"the market\". \"Hyggelig å møte deg\" is the full form of \"nice to meet you\".",
